   B-MODE (cross component), all radii:
      chi2 variation across the whole beta grid = 0.00
      the same on the TANGENTIAL component       = 106.29
   -> the cross component carries no lensing signal, so its profile
      in beta must be nearly FLAT.  A 'best-fitting' beta from a
      flat profile is meaningless -- the number that matters is how
      much chi2 beta buys, and on the B-mode that is 0.0 against
      106.3 on the real signal.

